{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_27_710954245#1_1445291041","relevance":2,"reason":"The result gives direct reasons some conservatives called for boycotting Starbucks, including its promise to hire 10,000 refugees, sensitivity training after the bathroom incident, and Democratic donations. However, it is a broader list of companies to boycott rather than a document dedicated specifically to why people boycott Starbucks.","learned":"Some conservative boycott calls against Starbucks cite refugee hiring, perceived virtue signaling/sensitivity training, and Democratic political donations."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ starbucks boycott veterans refugees)","reason":"Search the refugee/veterans controversy more specifically to find additional dedicated explanatory documents about backlash to Starbucks' refugee hiring pledge."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ starbucks boycott veterans refugees)"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_35_1302748456#3_3032038019","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q3323","rank":2,"snippet":"000000 , \"headings\": \"Does Starbucks ignore vets while helping refugees? Does Starbucks ignore vets while helping refugees?\" , \"segment\": \"Critics of Starbucks appear unaware of Starbucks’ track record with veterans. Twitter user @education4liberals and others have questioned why Starbucks should help <cover>refugees at a time when 50,000 homeless veterans are on the streets. That number, however, is out of date. Data from the U.S. Department of Housing and Urban Development estimates that about 39,500 veterans are homeless on any given night -- still too big of a group. Many homeless vets suffer from mental illness and may not be able to hold a job, according to the National Coalition for Homeless Veterans. #GrabYourWallet 00:30 Starbucks isn’t the only company feeling this sort of pressure. Since Donald Trump’s election, Kellogg ( K) has faced a boycott </cover>from the president’s supporters after it pulled its ads from Breitbart News, an ultraconservative website that has served as a platform for the white nationalist alt-right movement. Trump supporters have also called on consumers to quit doing business with Macy’s ( M) because the retailer wouldn’t promise to ","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_35_1302748456#0_3032032394","rank":1,"relevance":3}]}}
